cs-u1-q20.statement:
For integer \(i\) and array length \(n \ge  1\):

if \(i < 0\):       return \(0\)
else if \(i \ge  n\): return \(n - 1\)
else:          return \(i\)

In the final branch, which fact establishes that the returned index is valid?

cs-u2-q20.statement:
Each attempt below finishes, but may succeed or fail:

\(\mathrm{pending} = 3\)
while \(\mathrm{pending} > 0\):
    if \(\operatorname{attemptSucceeds}()\):
        \(\mathrm{pending} = \mathrm{pending} - 1\)

Does the fact that pending never increases establish termination?
